  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>mcp_list_tools - lists the tools of the Ridgeline Outfitters MCP server and reads its shipping policy
resource.
Needs the MCP connection retail-tools in your metastore (Transport Local process (stdio), Command
cmd, Arguments /c, python and the path to mcp-server\retail_mcp_server.py, one per line).

1. mcp-list-tools: MCP Client, connection retail-tools, Operation List tools; no input step; one row per tool
   with tool_name, tool_description, tool_schema.
2. txt-tools: Text file output, ${Internal.Entry.Current.Directory}/tools.csv: tool_name, tool_description,
   tool_schema.
3. gr-one-row: Generate rows, limit 1, no fields: the one row that makes mcp-shipping-policy read once.
4. mcp-shipping-policy: MCP Client, connection retail-tools, Operation Read resource, URI
   retail://policies/shipping; result field shipping_policy, error field resource_error.
5. wlog-shipping: Write to log, shipping_policy and resource_error.

Shipped data: the server offers 4 tools (lookup_order, check_stock, get_return_policy, start_return) and 1
resource; with Allowed tools set as in part 5 of the guide, List tools writes 3 rows.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>623</width>
      <heigth>296</heigth>
